{
  "title": "Popliteal Cyst in Children",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/pediatrics/4048/popliteal-cyst-in-children",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jun 14 2021",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Popliteal Cysts are common soft tissue masses in children that unlike the adult population, are most often not associated with meniscal tears.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is suspected clinically with a palpable mass in the popliteal fossa that transilluminates. MRI can confirm the diagnosis of a cystic lesion.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is observation as the majority of lesions spontaneously resolve.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Pathoanatomy",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "popliteal cysts usually are located",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "between muscles of",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "semimembranosus",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "medial head of gastrocnemius",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "from herniated posterior knee joint capsule synovium",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Muscles posterior to medial knee capsule",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "semimembranosus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "medial head of gastrocnemius",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually asymptomatic",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "located in popliteal fossa",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "usually located medially and distal to knee crease",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**most pronounced with knee extended**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "4",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "mass **will transilluminate**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
